{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#thm:dc-ch8-2-1","title":"thm:dc-ch8-2-1","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.md","line":429,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.tex#thm:dc-ch8-2-1","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#cor:dc-ch5-2-5]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.tex","label":"thm:dc-ch8-2-1","line":1212,"source":"\\begin{theorem}[Cartan local isometry theorem]\n  \\label{thm:dc-ch8-2-1}\n  \\uses{cor:dc-ch5-2-5, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging}\n\n  \\dcref{ch8:2.1}\n\n  With the notation above, if for all $q\\in V$ and all $x,y,u,v\\in T_q(M)$ we have\n\n\n  $$\n  \\langle R(x,y)u,v\\rangle=\\big\\langle\\tilde{R}(\\phi_t(x),\\phi_t(y))\\phi_t(u),\\phi_t(v)\\big\\rangle,\n  $$\n\n\n  then $f:V\\to f(V)\\subset\\tilde{M}$ is a local isometry and $df_p=i$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n  Let $q\\in V$ and let $\\gamma:[0,\\ell]\\to M$ be a normalized geodesic with\n  $\\gamma(0)=p$, $\\gamma(\\ell)=q$. Let $v\\in T_q(M)$ and let $J$ be a Jacobi field\n  along $\\gamma$ with $J(0)=0$ and $J(\\ell)=v$. Let $e_1,\\dots,e_n=\\gamma'(0)$ be an\n  orthonormal basis of $T_p(M)$ and let $e_i(t)$ be the parallel transport of $e_i$\n  along $\\gamma$. Writing $J(t)=\\sum_i y_i(t)e_i(t)$, the Jacobi equation gives\n\n\n  $$\n  y_j''+\\sum_i\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle y_i=0,\\qquad j=1,\\dots,n.\n  $$\n\n\n  Let $\\tilde{\\gamma}:[0,\\ell]\\to\\tilde{M}$ be the normalized geodesic with\n  $\\tilde{\\gamma}(0)=\\tilde{p}$, $\\tilde{\\gamma}'(0)=i(\\gamma'(0))$, and set\n  $\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi_t(J(t))$, $\\tilde{e}_j(t)=\\phi_t(e_j(t))$. By linearity of\n  $\\phi_t$, $\\tilde{J}(t)=\\sum_i y_i(t)\\tilde{e}_i(t)$. Since by hypothesis\n  $\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle=\\langle\\tilde{R}(\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_i)\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_j\\rangle$,\n  $\\tilde{J}$ satisfies the same equation, hence $\\tilde{J}$ is a Jacobi field along\n  $\\tilde{\\gamma}$ with $\\tilde{J}(0)=0$. Since parallel transport is an isometry,\n  $|\\tilde{J}(\\ell)|=|J(\\ell)|$. It remains to show that $\\tilde{J}(\\ell)=df_q(v)=df_q(J(\\ell))$.\n  Since $\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi_t(J(t))$, $\\tilde{J}'(0)=i(J'(0))$. Since $J$ and\n  $\\tilde{J}$ are Jacobi fields vanishing at $t=0$, by \\cref{cor:dc-ch5-2-5},\n\n\n  $$\n  J(t)=(d\\exp_p)_{t\\gamma'(0)}(tJ'(0)),\\qquad\\tilde{J}(t)=(d\\exp_{\\tilde{p}})_{t\\tilde{\\gamma}'(0)}(t\\tilde{J}'(0)).\n  $$\n\n\n  Therefore\n\n\n  $$\n  \\tilde{J}(\\ell)=(d\\exp_{\\tilde{p}})_{\\ell\\tilde{\\gamma}'(0)}\\circ i\\circ\\big((d\\exp_p)_{\\ell\\gamma'(0)}\\big)^{-1}(J(\\ell))=df_q(J(\\ell)),\n  $$\n\n\n  which proves the assertion.\n\n  If both exponential maps are global diffeomorphisms, the same argument makes $f$\n  a global isometry.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Theorem</div></section>[Cartan local isometry theorem] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-74686d3a64632d6368382d322d31\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23cor%3Adc-ch5-2-5\">↗ cor:dc-ch5-2-5</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-single-chart\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-phi\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-polarization\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch8:2.1</span></span><p></p>With the notation above, if for all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\in V$\">$q\\in V$</span> and all <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x,y,u,v\\in T_q(M)$\">$x,y,u,v\\in T_q(M)$</span> we have <p></p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\langle R(x,y)u,v\\rangle =\\big\\langle \\tilde{R}(\\phi _t(x),\\phi _t(y))\\phi _t(u),\\phi _t(v)\\big\\rangle ,  \\]\">\\[  \\langle R(x,y)u,v\\rangle =\\big\\langle \\tilde{R}(\\phi _t(x),\\phi _t(y))\\phi _t(u),\\phi _t(v)\\big\\rangle ,  \\]</span> <p></p>then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f:V\\to f(V)\\subset \\tilde{M}$\">$f:V\\to f(V)\\subset \\tilde{M}$</span> is a local isometry and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$df_p=i$\">$df_p=i$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q\\in V$\">$q\\in V$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[0,\\ell ]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[0,\\ell ]\\to M$</span> be a normalized geodesic with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (0)=p$\">$\\gamma (0)=p$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma (\\ell )=q$\">$\\gamma (\\ell )=q$</span>. Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_q(M)$\">$v\\in T_q(M)$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J$\">$J$</span> be a Jacobi field along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(0)=0$\">$J(0)=0$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(\\ell )=v$\">$J(\\ell )=v$</span>. Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_1,\\dots ,e_n=\\gamma &#x27;(0)$\">$e_1,\\dots ,e_n=\\gamma &#x27;(0)$</span> be an orthonormal basis of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_p(M)$\">$T_p(M)$</span> and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_i(t)$\">$e_i(t)$</span> be the parallel transport of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_i$\">$e_i$</span> along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span>. Writing <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J(t)=\\sum _i y_i(t)e_i(t)$\">$J(t)=\\sum _i y_i(t)e_i(t)$</span>, the Jacobi equation gives </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  y_j&#x27;&#x27;+\\sum _i\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle y_i=0,\\qquad j=1,\\dots ,n.  \\]\">\\[  y_j&#x27;&#x27;+\\sum _i\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle y_i=0,\\qquad j=1,\\dots ,n.  \\]</span></p><p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{\\gamma }:[0,\\ell ]\\to \\tilde{M}$\">$\\tilde{\\gamma }:[0,\\ell ]\\to \\tilde{M}$</span> be the normalized geodesic with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{\\gamma }(0)=\\tilde{p}$\">$\\tilde{\\gamma }(0)=\\tilde{p}$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{\\gamma }&#x27;(0)=i(\\gamma &#x27;(0))$\">$\\tilde{\\gamma }&#x27;(0)=i(\\gamma &#x27;(0))$</span>, and set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi _t(J(t))$\">$\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi _t(J(t))$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{e}_j(t)=\\phi _t(e_j(t))$\">$\\tilde{e}_j(t)=\\phi _t(e_j(t))$</span>. By linearity of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\phi _t$\">$\\phi _t$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}(t)=\\sum _i y_i(t)\\tilde{e}_i(t)$\">$\\tilde{J}(t)=\\sum _i y_i(t)\\tilde{e}_i(t)$</span>. Since by hypothesis <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle =\\langle \\tilde{R}(\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_i)\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_j\\rangle $\">$\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle =\\langle \\tilde{R}(\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_i)\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_j\\rangle $</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}$\">$\\tilde{J}$</span> satisfies the same equation, hence <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}$\">$\\tilde{J}$</span> is a Jacobi field along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{\\gamma }$\">$\\tilde{\\gamma }$</span> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}(0)=0$\">$\\tilde{J}(0)=0$</span>. Since parallel transport is an isometry, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$|\\tilde{J}(\\ell )|=|J(\\ell )|$\">$|\\tilde{J}(\\ell )|=|J(\\ell )|$</span>. It remains to show that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}(\\ell )=df_q(v)=df_q(J(\\ell ))$\">$\\tilde{J}(\\ell )=df_q(v)=df_q(J(\\ell ))$</span>. Since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi _t(J(t))$\">$\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi _t(J(t))$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}&#x27;(0)=i(J&#x27;(0))$\">$\\tilde{J}&#x27;(0)=i(J&#x27;(0))$</span>. Since <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$J$\">$J$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde{J}$\">$\\tilde{J}$</span> are Jacobi fields vanishing at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t=0$\">$t=0$</span>, by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh05_JacobiFields%23cor%3Adc-ch5-2-5\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#cor:dc-ch5-2-5\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-636f723a64632d6368352d322d35\">equation cor:dc-ch5-2-5</a>, </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  J(t)=(d\\exp _p)_{t\\gamma &#x27;(0)}(tJ&#x27;(0)),\\qquad \\tilde{J}(t)=(d\\exp _{\\tilde{p}})_{t\\tilde{\\gamma }&#x27;(0)}(t\\tilde{J}&#x27;(0)).  \\]\">\\[  J(t)=(d\\exp _p)_{t\\gamma &#x27;(0)}(tJ&#x27;(0)),\\qquad \\tilde{J}(t)=(d\\exp _{\\tilde{p}})_{t\\tilde{\\gamma }&#x27;(0)}(t\\tilde{J}&#x27;(0)).  \\]</span></p><p>Therefore </p><p><span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\tilde{J}(\\ell )=(d\\exp _{\\tilde{p}})_{\\ell \\tilde{\\gamma }&#x27;(0)}\\circ i\\circ \\big((d\\exp _p)_{\\ell \\gamma &#x27;(0)}\\big)^{-1}(J(\\ell ))=df_q(J(\\ell )),  \\]\">\\[  \\tilde{J}(\\ell )=(d\\exp _{\\tilde{p}})_{\\ell \\tilde{\\gamma }&#x27;(0)}\\circ i\\circ \\big((d\\exp _p)_{\\ell \\gamma &#x27;(0)}\\big)^{-1}(J(\\ell ))=df_q(J(\\ell )),  \\]</span></p><p>which proves the assertion. </p><p>If both exponential maps are global diffeomorphisms, the same argument makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> a global isometry. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-2-semiconjugacy","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#cor:dc-ch8-2-2","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#cor:dc-ch5-2-5","title":"cor:dc-ch5-2-5","label":"cor:dc-ch5-2-5"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#thm:dc-ch8-4-1","title":"thm:dc-ch8-4-1","label":"thm:dc-ch8-4-1"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#thm:dc-ch8-2-1","title":"thm:dc-ch8-2-1","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Cartan local isometry theorem]\n  \\label{thm:dc-ch8-2-1}\n  \\uses{cor:dc-ch5-2-5, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-single-chart, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-general, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-phi, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-transport-map, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-equiv, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-local-diffeo, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-polarization, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-mfderiv-bridge, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-diff-zero, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-reversal, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-backward-uniqueness, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-interior-data, lem:dc-ch8-2-1-local-isometry-packaging}\n\n  \\dcref{ch8:2.1}\n\n  With the notation above, if for all $q\\in V$ and all $x,y,u,v\\in T_q(M)$ we have\n\n\n  $$\n  \\langle R(x,y)u,v\\rangle=\\big\\langle\\tilde{R}(\\phi_t(x),\\phi_t(y))\\phi_t(u),\\phi_t(v)\\big\\rangle,\n  $$\n\n\n  then $f:V\\to f(V)\\subset\\tilde{M}$ is a local isometry and $df_p=i$.\n\\end{theorem}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n  Let $q\\in V$ and let $\\gamma:[0,\\ell]\\to M$ be a normalized geodesic with\n  $\\gamma(0)=p$, $\\gamma(\\ell)=q$. Let $v\\in T_q(M)$ and let $J$ be a Jacobi field\n  along $\\gamma$ with $J(0)=0$ and $J(\\ell)=v$. Let $e_1,\\dots,e_n=\\gamma'(0)$ be an\n  orthonormal basis of $T_p(M)$ and let $e_i(t)$ be the parallel transport of $e_i$\n  along $\\gamma$. Writing $J(t)=\\sum_i y_i(t)e_i(t)$, the Jacobi equation gives\n\n\n  $$\n  y_j''+\\sum_i\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle y_i=0,\\qquad j=1,\\dots,n.\n  $$\n\n\n  Let $\\tilde{\\gamma}:[0,\\ell]\\to\\tilde{M}$ be the normalized geodesic with\n  $\\tilde{\\gamma}(0)=\\tilde{p}$, $\\tilde{\\gamma}'(0)=i(\\gamma'(0))$, and set\n  $\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi_t(J(t))$, $\\tilde{e}_j(t)=\\phi_t(e_j(t))$. By linearity of\n  $\\phi_t$, $\\tilde{J}(t)=\\sum_i y_i(t)\\tilde{e}_i(t)$. Since by hypothesis\n  $\\langle R(e_n,e_i)e_n,e_j\\rangle=\\langle\\tilde{R}(\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_i)\\tilde{e}_n,\\tilde{e}_j\\rangle$,\n  $\\tilde{J}$ satisfies the same equation, hence $\\tilde{J}$ is a Jacobi field along\n  $\\tilde{\\gamma}$ with $\\tilde{J}(0)=0$. Since parallel transport is an isometry,\n  $|\\tilde{J}(\\ell)|=|J(\\ell)|$. It remains to show that $\\tilde{J}(\\ell)=df_q(v)=df_q(J(\\ell))$.\n  Since $\\tilde{J}(t)=\\phi_t(J(t))$, $\\tilde{J}'(0)=i(J'(0))$. Since $J$ and\n  $\\tilde{J}$ are Jacobi fields vanishing at $t=0$, by \\cref{cor:dc-ch5-2-5},\n\n\n  $$\n  J(t)=(d\\exp_p)_{t\\gamma'(0)}(tJ'(0)),\\qquad\\tilde{J}(t)=(d\\exp_{\\tilde{p}})_{t\\tilde{\\gamma}'(0)}(t\\tilde{J}'(0)).\n  $$\n\n\n  Therefore\n\n\n  $$\n  \\tilde{J}(\\ell)=(d\\exp_{\\tilde{p}})_{\\ell\\tilde{\\gamma}'(0)}\\circ i\\circ\\big((d\\exp_p)_{\\ell\\gamma'(0)}\\big)^{-1}(J(\\ell))=df_q(J(\\ell)),\n  $$\n\n\n  which proves the assertion.\n\n  If both exponential maps are global diffeomorphisms, the same argument makes $f$\n  a global isometry.\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch05_JacobiFields#cor:dc-ch5-2-5","title":"cor:dc-ch5-2-5","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-parallel-ortho-frame","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-transported-frame","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-hmatch-transfer","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-curvature-bridge","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-coeff-bridge","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-general","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-frame-chart-interface","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-norm-transfer-manifold","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#le